  "prefLabel": "Rev 206.03 Appeals",
  "priorExpiration": "2006-05-19",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 206.03 Appeals. Appeal of a final decision or order to the board of tax and land appeals or the superior court, in the county in which the taxpayer resides or has a place of business or resident agent, pursuant to RSA 21-J:28-b, shall be made within:\n\n(a) Thirty days of the final decision or order of the presiding officer, if no motion or petition is made pursuant to Rev 206.02; or\n\n(b) Thirty days of the decision of the presiding officer on a motion or petition made pursuant to Rev 206.02.\n\nSource. #4060, eff 5-29-86, EXPIRED: 5-29-92\n\nNew. #5423, eff 6-23-92; ss by #6749, eff 5-19-98, EXPIRED: 5-19-06\n\nNew. #8658-A, eff 6-13-06; ss by #11185-A, eff 9-20-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev200.html"
